    "result": "I've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n1. **generateReport** now accepts an optional `thresholds` object with metric IDs as keys and minimum scores as values\n2. Generates `passed` field (true if all thresholds pass, false if any fail)\n3. Includes `thresholds` array in the report with `{metric, min, score, passed}` entries for each threshold\n4. Metrics with no score (null) fail their thresholds\n\n### Reporters Updates\n- JSON reports include `passed` and `thresholds` fields when thresholds are provided\n- Markdown reports include a \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n- Both formats only include threshold data when thresholds are actually specified\n\n### CLI Updates (frai-cli)\n1. Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option that can be used multiple times\n2. Implemented threshold validation and parsing\n3. Exit codes:\n   - **0**: All thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified)\n   - **1**: One or more thresholds fail\n   - **2**: Malformed threshold or unknown metric (shows available metrics in error message)\n4. Reports are written either way and records the outcome\n\n### Tests\nAdded comprehensive tests for:\n- Passing thresholds\n- Failing thresholds\n- Missing metric scores (handled as failures)\n- Markdown report output with thresholds\n\nThe implementation works with both default metrics and custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`, as required for SDK users.\n\nReady to commit these changes. Would you like me to proceed?",
